    "body": "ShipStation has launched Ship with Walmart, giving Walmart Marketplace sellers access to Walmart-negotiated shipping rates and seller protections directly within its shipping platform. The service is available to ShipStation users and currently covers U.S. domestic shipments only.\nWhat’s Related\nSellers can activate Ship with Walmart, buy eligible shipping labels and manage Walmart Marketplace orders through their existing ShipStation account. It works alongside their existing carrier accounts as another shipping option, with no new integration to build.\nThe integration also includes up to $100 in protection for eligible lost-item claims on orders shipped on time. Walmart Marketplace orders appear alongside orders from Amazon , TikTok Shop, Shopify, eBay and other connected storefronts, allowing sellers to manage shipping from the same dashboard.\n“Sellers shouldn't have to choose between the tools they rely on every day and the benefits their marketplace offers them,” said Matt Norman, vice president of strategic business development at ShipStation. “Ship with Walmart closes that gap. Sellers get Walmart-negotiated rates and seller protections, including up to $100 of order protection, all within the ShipStation platform.”\nRELATED STORIES: Walmart to Convert Vacant Retail Space Into Delivery Depots | ShipStation Adds LTL Freight Shipping to Its Parcel Platform\nShipping benefits easy to access\nShip with Walmart gives sellers access to discounted rates from domestic carriers. After activation, they can purchase eligible labels directly in ShipStation while continuing to use their other shipping accounts.\nFor sellers handling orders from several marketplaces, the integration puts Walmart’s shipping benefits inside the software they already use to process orders. They can manage Walmart shipments alongside their other sales channels without leaving ShipStation.\nThe announcement does not identify participating carriers or specify the size of the label discounts. It also does not compare these rates with those available through sellers’ existing carrier accounts.\nProtection for lost-package claims\nThe lost-package protection covers eligible claims for packages lost in transit or after delivery , provided the orders were shipped on time. Sellers can also access negative feedback reviews for approved lost-item claims.\nShipStation says Ship with Walmart supports on-time delivery and valid tracking performance. Those features accompany the discounted labels and claim protections, though the announcement does not detail every eligibility requirement.\nCarrier recommendations and a subscription offer\nThe integration also brings Walmart’s Simplified Shipping Settings into ShipStation. The feature displays Walmart-recommended carriers and shipping service options based on the delivery promise the seller has made to the customer.\nWalmart Marketplace sellers new to ShipStation can receive 20% off their ShipStation subscription for one year when they activate Ship with Walmart. The subscription offer can be combined with discounted label rates, subject to eligibility requirements and offer terms.",
    "body_sha256": "96733b627398b8199188011c8ebb08a40de1ecbd826f0cf1e6abeeef51ac1087",
